 50    /** FUNCTION otap_plan.init_test
 51    * Provides the init_test functionality needed by otap_test and setting the package session variables.
 52    * Errors will get logged.
 53    *
 54    * @param p_test_count The amount of tests expected to be executed when called.
 55    * @param p_test_set The name of the test set applied if the name of the executed test procedure or function does not provide a test set name or name precendence is disabled.
 56    * @param p_test_group The name of the test group applied if the name of the executed test procedure or function does not provide a test group name or name precendence is disabled.
 57    * @param p_test_name The name of the test name applied if the name of the executed test procedure or function does not provide a test name or name precendence is disabled.
 58    * @param p_prefix The prefix to use for identifying test functions and procedures. Limited to 4 chars. Test functions and procedures must have a trailing delimiter _ after the prefix to be identified.
 59    * @param p_name_precedence Can disable the naming conventions for otap. If set to otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_FALSE, all tests will run under the defined test set and group, set by init_test.
 60    * @param p_include_pkg Can enable to search also packages and package procedures and functions that fit the naming convention with the given prefix, if set to otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_TRUE.
 61    * @param p_persist Can enable to persist the test results longer than the current default of PRESERVE_DAYS in OTAP_CONFIG, if set to otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_TRUE.
 62    * The following parameters are expected from OTAP_TEST package. Caller should not set this variables.
 63    * @param p_schema The current schema from caller environment as reported from otap_test.
 64    * @param p_user The current user from caller environment as reported from otap_test.
 65    * @param p_executor The session user from caller environment as reported from otap_test.
 66    * @param o_otap_session The OTAP_SESSION object to set.
 67    *
 68    * @return The current test session settings as text LF delimited.
 69    */
 70    FUNCTION init_test( p_test_count 	 IN	       NUMBER
 71  			 , p_test_set		 IN	       VARCHAR2
 72  			 , p_test_group 	 IN	       VARCHAR2
 73  			 , p_test_name		 IN	       VARCHAR2
 74  			 , p_prefix		 IN	       VARCHAR2
 75  			 , p_name_precedence	 IN	       NUMBER
 76  			 , p_include_pkg	 IN	       NUMBER
 77  			 , p_persist		 IN	       NUMBER
 78  			 , p_schema		 IN	       VARCHAR2
 79  			 , p_user		 IN	       VARCHAR2
 80  			 , p_executor		 IN	       VARCHAR2
 81  			 , o_otap_session	 IN OUT NOCOPY OTAP_SESSION
 82  			 )
