 86    /** FUNCTION otap_plan.run_tests
 87    * Identifies and runs test procedures. Test procedures are identified by a prefix with maximum 4 char length.
 88    * The prefix can be modified using otap_test.init_test. The delimiter for name components is always underline _.
 89    * The escape char used is backslash \. If name precedence is disabled, test set, group and test names are used
 90    * from the session record otherwise it tries to extract set, group and test name from the procedure name using
 91    * the session record entries as fallback name.
 92    *
 93    * The like expression is applied AFTER the prefix, complete search expression example with defaults: TEST\_%.
 94    *
 95    * As test procedure may manipulate the session record with test_init or test_finished, the resulting session
 96    * record is not reliable in sense of representing all tests. It represents only the last test run.
 97    *
 98    * Recommended usage: First run init_test, then call run_tests. In test procedures ensure that NO init_test or finish_test
 99    * occurs unless you persist the old test view results before executing finish_test or init_test. You may use the set functions
100    * for test set, group or name within the procedure. After run_tests finished, inspect the test views and persist your test
101    * results before executing init_test and run_tests again.
102    *
103    * @param p_like_expression The like expression (no regex) to limit further the procedures to run.
104    * @param p_schema_overwrite The alternate schema to use for finding test procedures. Will replace the current session value if NOT NULL.
105    * @param p_otap_session A valid OTAP_SESSION object to be used for test runs.
106    *
107    * @return A summary of the executed test procedures and session id at start of execution. Test summary can be found in the test views.
108    *
109    * @exception -20099 Internal error, invalid OTAP_SESSION object.
110    */
111    FUNCTION run_tests( p_like_expression   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT '%'
112  			 , p_schema_overwrite  IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL
113  			 , p_otap_session      IN OTAP_SESSION
114  			 )
115  	 RETURN VARCHAR2
116    ;
