391    /** FUNCTION otap_test.has_constraint
392    * Checks if a given table has a constraint of the given type. Optional you can specify column and constraint name.
393    *
394    * Supported constraint types:
395    * C - Check constraint on a table
396    * P - Primary key
397    * U - Unique key
398    * R - Referential integrity - use has_ref_constraint for more options
399    * V - With check option, on a view
400    * O - With read only, on a view
401    * H - Hash expression
402    * F - Constraint that involves a REF column - use has_ref_constraint for more options
403    * S is not supported, could not find or create an example to examine. SUPPLEMENTAL LOG clause only reflects in CDEF$ and CCOL$.
404    *
405    * @param p_table_name Mandatory. The table to be checked for constraint, take as is. Case sensitive. Missing value will cause test to fail.
406    * @param p_constraint_type Mandatory. A valid constraint type. Not case sensitive. Wrong values will cause the test to fail.
407    * @param p_column_name Optional. The column that is part of the constraint. Case sensitive.
408    * @param p_constraint Optional. The name of the constraint. Case sensitive.
409    * @param p_schema A schema override of the current test session if needed, taken as is. If given the table and constraint must exist in this schema. Case sensitive.
410    * @param p_description The test description if any. If not given, a description is generated, see template.
411    * @param p_expected_result The expected test result as number. Default is test passed. See otap_constants.
412    *
413    * @return The test result as text.
414    */
415    FUNCTION has_constraint( p_table_name	  IN VARCHAR2
416  			      , p_constraint_type IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'C'
417  			      , p_column_name	  IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL
418  			      , p_constraint	  IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL
419  			      , p_schema	  IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT SYS_CONTEXT('USERENV', 'CURRENT_SCHEMA')
420  			      , p_description	  IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL
421  			      , p_expected_result IN NUMBER   DEFAULT otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_TEST_PASSED
422  			      )
423  	 RETURN VARCHAR2
424    ;
