606    /** FUNCTION otap_test.generate_schema_tests
607    * Generates the test scripts for the current available otap schema functions using by default the current
608    * schema. Test set gets defined as schema, group represents the object types, like tables, triggers and so on.
609    * No translation provided. Limited to line size 4000 but not to rows, like DBMS_OUTPUT. It is up to you how you
610    * spool the content to files.
611    *
612    * Including system generated objects is a good idea if your system is stable and you want to ensure that no one
613    * changed the current state. With CI/CD or during development, when objects get recreated, it is a really bad idea.
614    * Excluded by default are objects beginning with SYS_ for system generated object or containing $ or # chars, which
615    * may occur anywhere in the name of system objects.
616    *
617    * There is no best option, some constraints like NOT NULL must be defined inline to count a column as NOT NULL.
618    * With an additional added constraint, the column will be still marked as NULLABLE. Identity columns are another
619    * issue, as you cannot define a name for the generated sequence. Make extra tests limited on the system generated
620    * objects you rely on (like NOT NULL and identity).
621    *
622    * @param p_like_schema The LIKE expression for schema names. Default is current schema. % will generate for all schemas in the database, be careful. Underlying objects are not limited. Case sensitive.
623    * @param p_title_prefix An optional title prefix for set, group and test names. Limited to 10 chars. Will be added without delimiter to the processed schema.
624    * @param p_show_header Used to surpress header comments, init, count and finish section. Default 1 will contain all sections, otherwise skipped.
625    * @param p_excl_sysgen Used to ignore system generated objects identified by SYS_, # or $. Default 1 will ignore system generated objects, otherwise included.
626    *
627    * @return An OTAP_VIEW_RESULT_REC object as table type OTAP_VIEW_RESULT_TBL.
628    */
629    FUNCTION generate_schema_tests( p_like_schema   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT SYS_CONTEXT('USERENV', 'CURRENT_SCHEMA')
630  				     , p_title_prefix  IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL
631  				     , p_show_header   IN INTEGER  DEFAULT otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_TRUE
632  				     , p_excl_sysgen   IN INTEGER  DEFAULT otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_TRUE
633  				     )
634  	 RETURN otap_view_result_tbl PIPELINED
635    ;
636  
